          "summary": "Limit Garman's ownership to its pre-existing Work, give Sparkling ownership of paid-for Modifications with a licence back to embedded Garman IP, and confirm Sparkling owns its data.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We have limited Garman's ownership to its pre-existing Software and Documentation, so that the Modifications and other work product we commission and pay for vest in us (with a perpetual licence back to any Garman IP embedded in them), and we have confirmed that we retain all rights in our data, including data converted under Section 4. Our playbook position is that we own what we fund and everything we put in, with no assignment of our IP or data to the vendor and no joint ownership; if Garman must retain title to modifications of its own code, we can accept a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free licence to use, modify and sublicense the Modifications for our business instead of the assignment.",
